                        "developer_response": "Hello Belphegore,\n\nPlease try again with the most recent version. We have upgraded the visuals, boosted the performance and save / load issues have been fixed. I hope you will now spend more time on the island and unlock additional endings. And ultimately find yourself liking the story as it is told.\n\nHowever, I have to respond regarding the \"previous titles being a mess part\":\n\n1. For Into the Dark, I take full responsibility. As in \"we have released 9 Patches for the Steam version, we released a free Halloween Bonus game each year, we provided 62 personal fixes for customers with special problems and we got 29 awards, including 4 Game of the Year awards for the game\".\nThe last patch was mere weeks ago, the next one weeks ahead. \n\n2. Regarding Painkiller Resurrection: Back in 2009, the publisher cut the development time by two months and force-released the first Beta as finished game, with the rest of our dev time being dedicated to the patch that should turn the first Beta into something playable. The funds allocated for that weren't payed out. As a matter of fact, we almost went into bankruptcy and lost ~ 20k Euros when Dreamcatcher went out of business. We worked an average of 80 hours per week FOR FREE to make it at least playable and broke down (mentally and physical) after this was done.",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1480102807,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
